.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-pipeline-upload - Upload URL for an archive build


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container pipeline upload   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Upload URL for an archive build

.PP
Returns a presigned \fBurl\fR (valid 15 minutes) for one \fBPUT\fR of exactly \fBsize\fR bytes (tar.gz / tgz / zip, max 200 MB; send \fBContent-Length: size\fR, e.g. \fBcurl -T site.tar.gz "<url>"\fR). Then start the build with \fBPOST .../runs {"upload_id": ...}\fR\&. Archives are deleted after 24 hours. Do not send an Idempotency-Key here (the URL would be withheld from the replayed answer).

.PP
API: POST /cloud/containers/{id}/pipelines/{pipeline}/uploads (operationId pipeline_upload, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for upload

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--size\fP=0
	archive size in bytes (1 - 209715200)


